.\"
.\" SYNC(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH SYNC 2 "January 2026" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
sync \- commit filesystem caches to disk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.B void sync(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sync ()
causes all pending modifications to filesystem metadata and cached
file data to be written to the underlying filesystems.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR sync ()
always succeeds.
.SH NOTES
.SS Substrate Native ABI
.nf
Syscall Number: 36
Arguments:      none
.fi
.SS Behavior
.BR sync ()
schedules writes but may return before the I/O is complete.
Use
.BR fsync (2)
or
.BR fdatasync (2)
for synchronous behavior on specific files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fsync (2),
.BR mount (2),
.BR substrate (7)
.SH STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2001, POSIX.1-2008.
